==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|aɪvə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang}} a [[banknote]] with a value of five, in the local currency
#* ''Do you have a '''fiver''' I could [[borrow]], I can pay you back tomorrow.
# by extension the value in money that this represents.
#* ''I bought the [[chocolate]]s, they were only a '''fiver'''.
# a clenched fist
# a mathematical puzzle played on a 5x5 grid
# {{context|Islam}} a [[Zaydi]] Shiite Muslim, who disagrees with the majority of Shiites on the identity of the Fifth Imam
# {{context|religion}} A person who gives five percent of their income or five hours a week of their time to charity (a reduction of ten percent [[tithing]])

